## 3. The render backend interface

`Render_Backend_Interface` (`render_backend_interface.odin`) is a `#all_or_none` struct of proc pointers, so a backend must fill in every field.

|   Group 			| 			Procs 										| 					Called from 				|
|-------------------|---------------------------------------------------	|-----------------------------------------------|
| Lifetime 			| `init`, `shutdown`        							| `init`, `shutdown` 							|
| Frame 			| `clear`, `draw`, `present` 							| `clear`, `draw_current_batch`, `present` 		|
| Swapchain 		| `resize_swapchain`, `get_swapchain_width/height` 		| resize events, `set_screen_size` |
| Textures 			| `create_texture`, `load_texture`, `update_texture`,   |
|                   | `destroy_texture`, `set_texture_filter`,              | texture and font procs, `draw_texture_fit`    | 
|					| `texture_needs_vertical_flip`                         |
| Render textures 	| `create_render_texture`, `destroy_render_target`      |    render texture procs                       |
| Shaders 			| `load_shader`, `destroy_shader`,                      | shader procs, `init`                          | 
|                   |  `default_shader_vertex_source`,                      | 
|					|  `default_shader_fragment_source`                     |
| Misc 				| `get_depth_clip_range`                                | `_update_projection_matrix`                   |

The data that crosses the interface on the hot path is small:

```odin
draw: proc(s: ^Render_Backend_State, vertex_buffer: []u8, draw_calls: []Draw_Call)
```

```odin
Draw_Call :: struct {
    vertex_offset: int,          // BYTE offset into vertex_buffer
    vertex_count:  int,
    shader:        Shader_Handle,
    vertex_size:   int,          // bytes per vertex for this shader
    constants:     []Shader_Constant_Location,   // offset+size of each constant in constants_data
    constants_data: []u8,        // snapshot of the shader's constants at the time of the draw call
    textures:      []Texture_Handle,             // one per shader texture bindpoint
    render_target: Render_Target_Handle,
    scissor:       Maybe(Rect),
    blend_mode:    Blend_Mode,
    changed:       bit_set[Draw_Call_Change],    // which of the above differ from the previous call
}
```

`changed` is what lets the backend skip redundant state setting. The interface comment also places a 
 duty on the backend: if it has to skip a draw call, it must carry that call's `changed` bits over to 
 the next one.

