## 6. Flushing a batch

`draw_current_batch` (`:814`):

```odin
if s.current_draw_call.vertex_count > 0 { append(&s.batch_draw_calls, s.current_draw_call) }

if len(s.batch_draw_calls) > 0 {
    _update_font_atlas()                                   // upload dirty glyph pixels first
    rb.draw(s.rb_state, s.vertex_buffer_cpu[:s.vertex_buffer_cpu_used], s.batch_draw_calls[:])
    clear(&s.batch_draw_calls)
}

s.current_draw_call = {}
s.draw_call_changes = DRAW_CALL_CHANGE_ALL                 // next batch re-sends all state
s.vertex_buffer_cpu_used = 0
free_all(s.batch_allocator)                                // drop the constants/texture snapshots
```

What triggers it:

| Trigger                                                                | Why                                          |
|   ---                                                                  | ---                                          |
| `present`                                                              | end of frame                                 |
| `clear`                                                                | pending draws must land before the clear     |
| vertex buffer full                                                     | make room                                    |
| `Event_Screen_Resize`, `Event_Window_Scale_Changed`, `set_screen_size` | pending draws were for the old swapchain     |
| `destroy_texture`, `update_texture`,                                   | only if the batch uses that texture          |
| `set_texture_filter*`, `destroy_font` (static)                          
| `destroy_shader`, `destroy_render_texture`                             | only if the batch uses that shader or target |
| dynamic font atlas full                                                | glyph positions are about to change          |

`present` (`:420`) is `draw_current_batch()`, `pf.before_present()` (a no-op on Windows), `rb.present()`.

